he Bar. The Central District’s Lawyer Representatives’\nL51@P1: Mediation Panel Selection Committee will assist the Court with the ADR Program\nL52@P1: in the following ways:\nL53@P1: (a) Recruit suitable candidates for the Mediation Panel;\nL54@P1: (b) Review candidate applications for the Mediation Panel and\nL55@P1: provide advice to the Court in connection with the selection and\nL56@P1-2: appointment of panel members; and1\nL57@P2: 2\nL58@P2: 3\nL59@P2: 4\nL60@P2: 5\nL61@P2: 6\nL62@P2: 7\nL63@P2: 8\nL64@P2: 9\nL65@P2: 10\nL66@P2: 11\nL67@P2: 12\nL68@P2: 13\nL69@P2: 14\nL70@P2: 15\nL71@P2: 16\nL72@P2: 17\nL73@P2: 18\nL74@P2: 19\nL75@P2: 20\nL76@P2: 21\nL77@P2: 22\nL78@P2: 23\nL79@P2: 24\nL80@P2: 25\nL81@P2: 26\nL82@P2: 27\nL83@P2: 28\nL84@P2: General Order No. 11-10\nL85@P2: 3\nL86@P2: (c) Perform such additional duties as the Court may direct which are\nL87@P2: necessary for the efficient administration of the ADR Program.\nL88@P2: 3. MEDIATOR QUALIFICATIONS AND SELECTION\nL89@P2: 3.1 Qualifications. A person may serve as a member of the Mediation\nL90@P2: Panel if:\nL91@P2: (a) the person has been a United States Appellate, District,\nL92@P2: Magistrate or Bankruptcy Judge, or a California Judicial Officer;\nL93@P2: or\nL94@P2: (b) the person is currently a member in good standing of the Bar of\nL95@P2: the United States District Court, Central District of California,\nL96@P2: with at least 10 years legal practice experience, substantial\nL97@P2: experience with or knowledge of civil litigation in federal court,\nL98@P2: and significant expertise in one or more of the following areas:\nL99@P2: (1) Admiralty\nL100@P2: (2) Americans with Disabilities Act\nL101@P2: (3) Antitrust\nL102@P2: (4) Bankruptcy\nL103@P2: (5) Business/Commercial Litigation\nL104@P2: (6) Civil Rights\nL105@P2: (7) Class Actions\nL106@P2: (8) Consumer Credit\nL107@P2: (9) Copyright/Trademark\nL108@P2: (10) Employment/Discrimination/Wrongful Termination\nL109@P2: (11) Environmental\nL110@P2: (12) ERISA\nL111@P2: (13) Foreclosure\nL112@P2-3: (14) Insurance Coverage/Bad Faith1\nL113@P3: 2\nL114@P3: 3\nL115@P3: 4\nL116@P3: 5\nL117@P3: 6\nL118@P3: 7\nL119@P3: 8\nL120@P3: 9\nL121@P3: 10\nL122@P3: 11\nL123@P3: 12\nL124@P3: 13\nL125@P3: 14\nL126@P3: 15\nL127@P3: 16\nL128@P3: 17\nL129@P3: 18\nL130@P3: 19\nL131@P3: 20\nL132@P3: 21\nL133@P3: 22\nL134@P3: 23\nL135@P3: 24\nL136@P3: 25\nL137@P3: 26\nL138@P3: 27\nL139@P3: 28\nL140@P3: General Order No. 11-10\nL141@P3: 4\nL142@P3: (15) Labor\nL143@P3: (16) Patent\nL144@P3: (17) Personal Injury\nL145@P3: (18) Products Liability\nL146@P3: (19) Real Estate/Construction\nL147@P3: (20) Securities\nL148@P3: (21) Tax\nL149@P3: The Court may modify these and other minimum requirements in individual\nL150@P3: circumstances for good cause. The Court shall only make such modification upon a\nL151@P3: determination that the applicant has demonstrated satisfactory evidence of sufficient\nL152@P3: education, training, skills and/or experience.\nL153@P3: 3.2 Training Requirements. In order to qualify for appointment to the\nL154@P3: Mediation Panel, an applicant shall successfully complete a court-conducted\nL155@P3: training course in mediation or provide proof that he or she has successfully\nL156@P3: completed a court-approved training course in mediation. In order to qualify for\nL157@P3: subsequent reappointments to the Mediation Panel, an applicant shall agree to\nL158@P3: periodically participate in court-conducted or court-approved refresher or advanced\nL159@P3: training. The Court may, in its discretion, waive the training requirements upon\nL160@P3: application by the individual.\nL161@P3: 3.3 Application for Appointment to Mediation Panel. An application\nL162@P3: for appointment to the Mediation Panel may be obtained from the ADR Program\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGO 25-05.pdf (https://www.cacd.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/general-orders/GO%2025-05.pdf)\ncite